Priya Rao: Quick heads-up — Lumen Health goes live tomorrow. Want a lightweight priming + streaming fallback runbook we can hand to SRE/CS. Focus: small prefill to warm caches, simple batching thresholds, streaming enabled but graceful fallback if latency spikes. Sharing draft runbook below.

Jordan Lee: SGTM. Two asks: limit prefill rate so we don't burst capacity, and ensure we have an explicit consent/opt-out flag for PII-sensitive tenants.

Priya Rao: Agreed. Proposed parameters: prefill window = 10m before first live request; max prefill rate = 5 prefill requests/min per tenant; batch_size = 8; parallel_workers = 2; KV cache prefix = tenant:lumen-123:*; KV TTL = 15m for warm-pool entries. If 95th p95 token latency > 500ms during warm, automatically disable streaming for that tenant and route to non-streamed endpoint.

Alex Chen: Add telemetry markers: prefill_requested, prefill_success, cache_hit, stream_enabled, stream_fallback, and onboarding_risk. CS should own the mapping for onboarding_risk signals.

Nate Kim: For renewal risk capture, CS will flag an account as onboarding_risk:true when either: (a) utilization < 10% of expected by day 7, or (b) sustained error_rate > 3% for 24h post-go-live. We'll expose a small webhook field on the account object (onboard_risk) that tooling can update. Ops/SRE can subscribe to that signal to avoid aggressive autoscaling for risky tenants.

Jordan Lee: Quick manual trigger for ops (curl) so SRE can kick prefill if needed:

```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/prefill \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"tenant_id":"lumen-123","prompts":["init","profile-scan"],"batch_size":8}'
```

Priya Rao: Client guidance (share with customer): use SSE with exponential backoff for dropped connections, accept partial results as valid for UI progressive render. Example JS backoff snippet for the SDK:

```
let attempts = 0;
function connectSSE() {
  const s = new EventSource(url);
  s.onopen = () => { attempts = 0; };
  s.onerror = () => {
    s.close();
    attempts++;
    setTimeout(connectSSE, Math.min(30000, 1000 * 2 ** attempts));
  };
}
connectSSE();
```

CS-Bot: Reminder: runbook draft saved in Confluence -> https://rw-internal.atlassian.net/lumen-prefill (permissions: customer-success, eng-runtime).

Alex Chen: Action items: Jordan — create the final short-runbook in docs and include the cURL + JS snippets; Nate — wire the onboarding_risk webhook and add two telemetry metrics to the metrics catalog; Priya — schedule a 15-min kickoff with Lumen to walk through consent, rollback plan, and renewal-touch template. I'll draft the renewal outreach email template and share it after kickoff.

Priya Rao: Thanks team — @Jordan can you post the final runbook here by EOD? :thumbsup:
